  "title": "Concavity of van der Waerden numbers",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For $k$ and $\\ell$ positive integers, the (mixed) van der Waerden number $w(k,\\ell)$ is the least positive integer $n$ such that every (red-blue)-coloring of $[1,n]$ admits either a $k$-term red arithmetic progression or an $\\ell$-term blue arithmetic progression.\n\nConjecture For all $k$ and $\\ell$ with $k \\geq \\ell$, $w(k,\\ell) \\geq w(k+1,\\ell-1)$.",
